  "preamble": "Vocalization of a voiced velar stop to a high front vocoid, usually the offglide [i̯] of a new diphthong. The change passes through a fricative or glide stage ([ɣ] > [j] > [i̯]). In western Romance, Latin g before a consonant vocalized in this way; in English, Proto-Germanic *g after front vowels became Old English ġ [j], which merged with the preceding vowel as a diphthong in Middle English.",
